Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Mystery solved!

The git source isn't up to date.  If you download the latest package
then git the latest source you will discover the main.cc files are
different.  Replacing the main.cc from the latest package direct
download in the git repository download corrects the problem.  All
adds up now.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
jrounds@jrlaptop:~$ git clone git://github.com/saptarshiguha/RHIPE.git <http://github.com/saptarshiguha/RHIPE.git>
Initialized empty Git repository in /home/jrounds/RHIPE/.git/
remote: Counting objects: 3081, done.
remote: Compressing objects: 100% (909/909), done.
remote: Total 3081 (delta 2094), reused 2951 (delta 2031)
Receiving objects: 100% (3081/3081), 9.28 MiB | 283 KiB/s, done.
Resolving deltas: 100% (2094/2094), done.
jrounds@jrlaptop:~$ diff '/home/jrounds/RHIPE/code/R/src/main.cc' '/
home/jrounds/Downloads/Rhipe/src/main.cc'
123a124
> #ifdef RHIPEDEBUG
129,130c130
<     snprintf(fn,10234,"/tmp/rhipe.euid-%d.pid-%d.log",uid,getpid());
< #ifdef RHIPEDEBUG
---
>     snprintf(fn,1023,"/tmp/rhipe.euid-%d.pid-%d.log",uid,getpid());

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The buggy sprintfs behind the debug #ifdef are still before it in the
git source. Thank you for a very interesting package!  Now... I can
start tinkering!

Jeremiah

